WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
positron has a package pane for managing the packages that are installed in your

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:09.520
active R or Python sessions. So you can browse installed packages, search package

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:14.640
repositories, and update or uninstall packages without ever leaving positron.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:19.760
The packages pane appears in the primary sidebar and you can select the icon in

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.280
the activity bar or you can run view packages from the command palette. The

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.840
packages pane lists packages installed in the active session library and so

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:33.320
each entry shows a package name, version, and whether or not the package is

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.119
currently attached. There are also buttons to open up the packages

00:00:37.119 --> 00:00:42.279
documentation in the help pane and when a package has a documentation site its

00:00:42.279 --> 00:00:46.240
website in your browser. So you can use the filter input at the top of the pane

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:51.400
to search by name. So for example here I can search for ggplot2 and see that

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:56.680
there's an update available and update it just directly from here. Or if I want

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:00.840
to install patchwork in my script, I can search for patchwork and install it

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:05.400
into the active session. So all of these actions are available from the command

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.800
palette. What you do is you type packages to see the full list, so all the commands

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:17.279
for installing, updating, uninstalling, and refreshing packages. Give it a try today!

